avformat/mpegtsenc: write the Dolby Vision descriptors

The demuxer reads the DOVI video stream descriptor (0xb0) into the
stream's AV_PKT_DATA_DOVI_CONF record, but the muxer never wrote it. A
Dolby Vision stream copied from one transport stream into another
therefore kept every RPU NAL unit and lost its configuration record,
and a player that recognises Dolby Vision from the record treats the
copy as HDR10 (Profile 8.1), HLG (Profile 8.4) or, for Profile 5, as
HDR10 with the wrong colours, because IPT-PQ-c2 is then decoded as
YCbCr. AetherEngine's live recordings stream-copy into MPEG-TS and hit
exactly that.

This is the muxer half of the upstream submission (FFmpeg PR 26097,
second round), ported to n8.1.3. For an H.264 or HEVC stream whose
record carries both its base layer and its RPU, the muxer writes the
DOVI video stream descriptor from "Dolby Vision Streams Within the
MPEG-2 Transport Stream Format" v1.2, and for compatibility ID 0
(Profile 5) also the 'DOVI' registration descriptor, as section 7.1.2
asks. Both go before the codec registration, because the demuxer keeps
the last registration as codec_tag. Profile 5 keeps stream_type 0x24
instead of the 0x06 of 7.1.2, since players that do not know Dolby
Vision lose the video with 0x06. The last byte carries
dv_md_compression where the demuxer reads it.

Not covered: an enhancement layer on its own PID, which needs its base
layer's PID. The upstream PMT size check is not part of this port: it
guards the LCEVC linkage descriptor, which n8.1.3 does not write, and
the at most 13 new bytes fit the existing 32-byte margin.

